digraph GSN {
  rankdir=TB;
  node [fontname="Helvetica" fontsize=9];
  edge [fontname="Helvetica" fontsize=8];
  labelloc="t"; label="SafeDSE safety argument — f_random_hw"; fontname="Helvetica";
  C1 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C1\nIEC 61508 is the governing functional\nsafety standard; integrity is allocated as\na Safety Integrity Level per actor (Q1,\nQ13)."];
  C2 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C2\nPlatform: 22 core slots across 7 fault\ncontainment regions, core types cortexM,\ncortexR. Cores actually instantiated in\nthis solution: [1, 3, 7, 8, 9]."];
  C3 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C3\nApplications: c_rasta, modelled as\nsynchronous dataflow graphs and unfolded\nto an equivalent homogeneous graph before\nmapping."];
  C4 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C4\nFault model under consideration: random\nhardware faults (Q2). Patterns not\ncovering this fault class were excluded\nfrom the design space, and placement\nrelations motivated only by an excluded\nfault class were not posted."];
  J1 [shape=ellipse style=filled fillcolor="#fff6d5" label="J1 (J)\nThis argument is generated from a design\nspace exploration result. It argues only\nover properties of the ARCHITECTURE and\nits DEPLOYMENT: which pattern is applied\nto which actor, where components are\nplaced relative to each other, how\nintegrity levels are provisioned per core,\nand whether the resulting schedule meets\nits timing requirement. Claims about\nimplementation correctness, detection\ncoverage and development process are\noutside what a mapping can establish and\nare carried below as undeveloped goals."];
  A1 [shape=ellipse style=filled fillcolor="#fff6d5" label="A1 (A)\nThe worst-case execution times supplied to\nthe exploration are sound upper bounds for\nevery actor on every core type it may be\nbound to. The exploration consumes these\nfigures; it does not establish them."];
  A2 [shape=ellipse style=filled fillcolor="#fff6d5" label="A2 (A)\nToken preservation (Q4): every replica\nfires on every iteration and produces on\nall of its outputs, in the fault-free and\nin the degraded case alike. Detection\nmarks a token invalid; it never withholds\none. The timing argument therefore holds\nin the degraded mode, at the cost of being\nconservative when no fault is present."];
  G1 [shape=box label="G1\nThe deployed architecture of f_random_hw\npreserves the allocated safety integrity\nof every safety-related actor."];
  S1 [shape=parallelogram label="S1\nArgument over each safety-related actor in\nturn, followed by the platform-wide\nproperties on which those per-actor\narguments depend."];
  G2 [shape=box label="G2\nActor frontEnd of application c_rasta,\nallocated SIL 3, attains SIL 3 in the\ndeployed architecture."];
  C5 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C5\nfrontEnd is unfolded into 1 concurrent\ncopy, bound to core 1, implemented at SIL\n3."];
  Sn1 [shape=circle label="Sn1\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nevery active copy of frontEnd is\nimplemented at or above its allocated SIL\nand runs on a core provisioned to at least\nthat level."];
  G3 [shape=box label="G3\nEvery copy of frontEnd is implemented at\nSIL 3 or above and is not hosted on a core\nprovisioned below that level."];
  C6 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C6\nComponents introduced by\nhigh_sil_isolated_checker for frontEnd:\nchecker on core 3 at SIL 3."];
  S2 [shape=parallelogram label="S2\nArgument by application of the\nhigh_sil_isolated_checker safety\narchitecture pattern, over each of its\ngeneral scenarios."];
  C7 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C7\nPattern high_sil_isolated_checker\n[koopman, High SIL Doer/Checker with\nisolated checker]: A high-SIL doer with an\nequally high-SIL checker on a separate\nprocessor. Distinct from the SIL 1-2\nDoer/Checker family in that both sides are\ndeveloped to the high level, and from\n2-of-2 in that the checker verifies rather\nthan recomputes -- so its WCET is a\nfraction of the doer's, which is what\nmakes it competitive on throughput.\nKoopman's 'Attempted High SIL\nDoer/Checker' is the same structure\nWITHOUT the isolation, and is an\nanti-pattern; the C.4 check rejects any\nrecord that claims to fail silent while\nco-locating its channels. Attainable SIL\n[3]; covers random_hw; fails silent; voter\nfolded."];
  G4 [shape=box label="G4\nAn implausible output of the doer is\ndetected by the equally-high-SIL checker.\n[high_sil_isolated_checker/SC1]"];
  S3 [shape=parallelogram label="S3\nAchieved through the Sanity Check tactic\n(Checking): Detection of implausible\nsystem outputs or states."];
  C8 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C8\nSanity Check: Checks whether a system\nstate or value remains within a valid\nrange which can be defined in the system\nspecification or which is based on\nknowledge about the internal structure or\nnature of the system."];
  C9 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C9\nCandidate methods from the standard: IEC\n61508-7 A.1.2 monitoring relay contacts;\nIEC 61508-7 A.2.7 analog signal\nmonitoring; IEC 61508-7 A.3.1-A.3.3\nself-tests; IEC 61508-7 A.4.1-A.4.4\nchecksums; IEC 61508-7 A.5.1-A.5.5 RAM\ntests; IEC 61508-7 A.6.1 test pattern; IEC\n61508-7 A.9 temporal and logical program\nmonitoring; IEC 61508-7 C.3.3 assertion\nprogramming; IEC 61508-7 C.5.3 interface\nchecking"];
  G5 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G5\nAn IEC 61508 method realising Sanity Check\nis implemented in frontEnd, and its\neffectiveness for the faults of concern is\ndemonstrated.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G6 [shape=box label="G6\nA random hardware fault in the doer's\nfault containment region does not disable\nthe checker.\n[high_sil_isolated_checker/SC2]"];
  S4 [shape=parallelogram label="S4\nAchieved through the Replication\nRedundancy tactic (Redundancy):\nIntroduction of a redundant system which\nallows detection or masking of random\nhardware failures (not systematic\nfailures)."];
  C10 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C10\nReplication Redundancy: Introduction of a\nredundant system of the same\nimplementation. The redundant systems\nmaintain the same functionality, use\nidentical hardware, and run the same\nsoftware implementation."];
  G7 [shape=box label="G7\nIn the deployed mapping, the replicated\ncomponents are deployed on hardware that\ndoes not share a single point of random\nhardware failure."];
  Sn2 [shape=circle label="Sn2\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nDIFFERENT_FCR between frontEnd and\nfrontEnd/checker: cores 1/3, fault\ncontainment regions 1/2, core types\ncortexR/cortexR."];
  C11 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C11\nCandidate methods from the standard: IEC\n61508-7 A.2.1 tests by redundant hardware;\nIEC 61508-7 A.2.5 monitored redundancy;\nIEC 61508-7 A.3.5 reciprocal comparison by\nsoftware; IEC 61508-7 A.4.5 block\nreplication; IEC 61508-7 A.6.3\nmulti-channel output; IEC 61508-7 A.7.3\ncomplete hardware redundancy; IEC 61508-7\nA.7.5 transmission redundancy"];
  G8 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G8\nAn IEC 61508 method realising Replication\nRedundancy is implemented in frontEnd, and\nits effectiveness for the faults of\nconcern is demonstrated.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G9 [shape=box label="G9\nActor rasta of application c_rasta,\nallocated SIL 1, attains SIL 1 in the\ndeployed architecture."];
  C12 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C12\nrasta is unfolded into 1 concurrent copy,\nbound to core 7, implemented at SIL 1."];
  Sn3 [shape=circle label="Sn3\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nevery active copy of rasta is implemented\nat or above its allocated SIL and runs on\na core provisioned to at least that level."];
  G10 [shape=box label="G10\nEvery copy of rasta is implemented at SIL\n1 or above and is not hosted on a core\nprovisioned below that level."];
  S5 [shape=parallelogram label="S5\nArgument by development process alone: no\nstructural safety pattern is applied."];
  C13 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C13\nIEC 61508 expects diagnostic coverage from\nSIL 2 upward, so process alone is\nadmissible only to SIL 1 (Q20). The\nexploration enforced this ceiling when\nchoosing the pattern."];
  G11 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G11\nrasta is developed and verified to SIL 1\nin accordance with IEC 61508-3.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G12 [shape=box label="G12\nActor powspec of application c_rasta,\nallocated SIL 1, attains SIL 1 in the\ndeployed architecture."];
  C14 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C14\npowspec is unfolded into 1 concurrent\ncopy, bound to core 7, implemented at SIL\n1."];
  Sn4 [shape=circle label="Sn4\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nevery active copy of powspec is\nimplemented at or above its allocated SIL\nand runs on a core provisioned to at least\nthat level."];
  G13 [shape=box label="G13\nEvery copy of powspec is implemented at\nSIL 1 or above and is not hosted on a core\nprovisioned below that level."];
  S6 [shape=parallelogram label="S6\nArgument by development process alone: no\nstructural safety pattern is applied."];
  C15 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C15\nIEC 61508 expects diagnostic coverage from\nSIL 2 upward, so process alone is\nadmissible only to SIL 1 (Q20). The\nexploration enforced this ceiling when\nchoosing the pattern."];
  G14 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G14\npowspec is developed and verified to SIL 1\nin accordance with IEC 61508-3.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G15 [shape=box label="G15\nActor audspec of application c_rasta,\nallocated SIL 1, attains SIL 1 in the\ndeployed architecture."];
  C16 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C16\naudspec is unfolded into 1 concurrent\ncopy, bound to core 7, implemented at SIL\n1."];
  Sn5 [shape=circle label="Sn5\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nevery active copy of audspec is\nimplemented at or above its allocated SIL\nand runs on a core provisioned to at least\nthat level."];
  G16 [shape=box label="G16\nEvery copy of audspec is implemented at\nSIL 1 or above and is not hosted on a core\nprovisioned below that level."];
  S7 [shape=parallelogram label="S7\nArgument by development process alone: no\nstructural safety pattern is applied."];
  C17 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C17\nIEC 61508 expects diagnostic coverage from\nSIL 2 upward, so process alone is\nadmissible only to SIL 1 (Q20). The\nexploration enforced this ceiling when\nchoosing the pattern."];
  G17 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G17\naudspec is developed and verified to SIL 1\nin accordance with IEC 61508-3.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G18 [shape=box label="G18\nActor compJah of application c_rasta,\nallocated SIL 3, attains SIL 3 in the\ndeployed architecture."];
  C18 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C18\ncompJah is unfolded into 1 concurrent\ncopy, bound to core 1, implemented at SIL\n3."];
  Sn6 [shape=circle label="Sn6\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nevery active copy of compJah is\nimplemented at or above its allocated SIL\nand runs on a core provisioned to at least\nthat level."];
  G19 [shape=box label="G19\nEvery copy of compJah is implemented at\nSIL 3 or above and is not hosted on a core\nprovisioned below that level."];
  C19 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C19\nComponents introduced by\nhigh_sil_isolated_checker for compJah:\nchecker on core 3 at SIL 3."];
  S8 [shape=parallelogram label="S8\nArgument by application of the\nhigh_sil_isolated_checker safety\narchitecture pattern, over each of its\ngeneral scenarios."];
  C20 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C20\nPattern high_sil_isolated_checker\n[koopman, High SIL Doer/Checker with\nisolated checker]: A high-SIL doer with an\nequally high-SIL checker on a separate\nprocessor. Distinct from the SIL 1-2\nDoer/Checker family in that both sides are\ndeveloped to the high level, and from\n2-of-2 in that the checker verifies rather\nthan recomputes -- so its WCET is a\nfraction of the doer's, which is what\nmakes it competitive on throughput.\nKoopman's 'Attempted High SIL\nDoer/Checker' is the same structure\nWITHOUT the isolation, and is an\nanti-pattern; the C.4 check rejects any\nrecord that claims to fail silent while\nco-locating its channels. Attainable SIL\n[3]; covers random_hw; fails silent; voter\nfolded."];
  G20 [shape=box label="G20\nAn implausible output of the doer is\ndetected by the equally-high-SIL checker.\n[high_sil_isolated_checker/SC1]"];
  S9 [shape=parallelogram label="S9\nAchieved through the Sanity Check tactic\n(Checking): Detection of implausible\nsystem outputs or states."];
  C21 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C21\nSanity Check: Checks whether a system\nstate or value remains within a valid\nrange which can be defined in the system\nspecification or which is based on\nknowledge about the internal structure or\nnature of the system."];
  C22 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C22\nCandidate methods from the standard: IEC\n61508-7 A.1.2 monitoring relay contacts;\nIEC 61508-7 A.2.7 analog signal\nmonitoring; IEC 61508-7 A.3.1-A.3.3\nself-tests; IEC 61508-7 A.4.1-A.4.4\nchecksums; IEC 61508-7 A.5.1-A.5.5 RAM\ntests; IEC 61508-7 A.6.1 test pattern; IEC\n61508-7 A.9 temporal and logical program\nmonitoring; IEC 61508-7 C.3.3 assertion\nprogramming; IEC 61508-7 C.5.3 interface\nchecking"];
  G21 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G21\nAn IEC 61508 method realising Sanity Check\nis implemented in compJah, and its\neffectiveness for the faults of concern is\ndemonstrated.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G22 [shape=box label="G22\nA random hardware fault in the doer's\nfault containment region does not disable\nthe checker.\n[high_sil_isolated_checker/SC2]"];
  S10 [shape=parallelogram label="S10\nAchieved through the Replication\nRedundancy tactic (Redundancy):\nIntroduction of a redundant system which\nallows detection or masking of random\nhardware failures (not systematic\nfailures)."];
  C23 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C23\nReplication Redundancy: Introduction of a\nredundant system of the same\nimplementation. The redundant systems\nmaintain the same functionality, use\nidentical hardware, and run the same\nsoftware implementation."];
  G23 [shape=box label="G23\nIn the deployed mapping, the replicated\ncomponents are deployed on hardware that\ndoes not share a single point of random\nhardware failure."];
  Sn7 [shape=circle label="Sn7\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nDIFFERENT_FCR between compJah and\ncompJah/checker: cores 1/3, fault\ncontainment regions 1/2, core types\ncortexR/cortexR."];
  C24 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C24\nCandidate methods from the standard: IEC\n61508-7 A.2.1 tests by redundant hardware;\nIEC 61508-7 A.2.5 monitored redundancy;\nIEC 61508-7 A.3.5 reciprocal comparison by\nsoftware; IEC 61508-7 A.4.5 block\nreplication; IEC 61508-7 A.6.3\nmulti-channel output; IEC 61508-7 A.7.3\ncomplete hardware redundancy; IEC 61508-7\nA.7.5 transmission redundancy"];
  G24 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G24\nAn IEC 61508 method realising Replication\nRedundancy is implemented in compJah, and\nits effectiveness for the faults of\nconcern is demonstrated.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G25 [shape=box label="G25\nActor rastaFilter of application c_rasta,\nallocated SIL 1, attains SIL 1 in the\ndeployed architecture."];
  C25 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C25\nrastaFilter is unfolded into 1 concurrent\ncopy, bound to core 7, implemented at SIL\n1."];
  Sn8 [shape=circle label="Sn8\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nevery active copy of rastaFilter is\nimplemented at or above its allocated SIL\nand runs on a core provisioned to at least\nthat level."];
  G26 [shape=box label="G26\nEvery copy of rastaFilter is implemented\nat SIL 1 or above and is not hosted on a\ncore provisioned below that level."];
  S11 [shape=parallelogram label="S11\nArgument by development process alone: no\nstructural safety pattern is applied."];
  C26 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C26\nIEC 61508 expects diagnostic coverage from\nSIL 2 upward, so process alone is\nadmissible only to SIL 1 (Q20). The\nexploration enforced this ceiling when\nchoosing the pattern."];
  G27 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G27\nrastaFilter is developed and verified to\nSIL 1 in accordance with IEC 61508-3.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G28 [shape=box label="G28\nActor backEnd of application c_rasta,\nallocated SIL 2, attains SIL 2 in the\ndeployed architecture."];
  C27 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C27\nbackEnd is unfolded into 1 concurrent\ncopy, bound to core 8, implemented at SIL\n2."];
  Sn9 [shape=circle label="Sn9\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nevery active copy of backEnd is\nimplemented at or above its allocated SIL\nand runs on a core provisioned to at least\nthat level."];
  G29 [shape=box label="G29\nEvery copy of backEnd is implemented at\nSIL 2 or above and is not hosted on a core\nprovisioned below that level."];
  C28 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C28\nComponents introduced by\nlow_sil_doer_checker for backEnd: checker\non core 9 at SIL 2."];
  S12 [shape=parallelogram label="S12\nArgument by application of the\nlow_sil_doer_checker safety architecture\npattern, over each of its general\nscenarios."];
  C29 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C29\nPattern low_sil_doer_checker [koopman, Low\nSIL Doer/Checker Pair (E-quizzer)]: A\nlow-SIL doer on one CPU, checked by a\nhigher-SIL checker on a SEPARATE CPU. The\nchecker quizzes the doer and can shut the\nchannel down, so the pair fails active at\nSIL 1-2. Separation is what makes it\ntolerate a random hardware fault in the\ndoer's processor. Attainable SIL [1, 2];\ncovers random_hw; fails active; voter\nfolded."];
  G30 [shape=box label="G30\nAn implausible output of the doer is\ndetected by the checker.\n[low_sil_doer_checker/SC1]"];
  S13 [shape=parallelogram label="S13\nAchieved through the Sanity Check tactic\n(Checking): Detection of implausible\nsystem outputs or states."];
  C30 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C30\nSanity Check: Checks whether a system\nstate or value remains within a valid\nrange which can be defined in the system\nspecification or which is based on\nknowledge about the internal structure or\nnature of the system."];
  C31 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C31\nCandidate methods from the standard: IEC\n61508-7 A.1.2 monitoring relay contacts;\nIEC 61508-7 A.2.7 analog signal\nmonitoring; IEC 61508-7 A.3.1-A.3.3\nself-tests; IEC 61508-7 A.4.1-A.4.4\nchecksums; IEC 61508-7 A.5.1-A.5.5 RAM\ntests; IEC 61508-7 A.6.1 test pattern; IEC\n61508-7 A.9 temporal and logical program\nmonitoring; IEC 61508-7 C.3.3 assertion\nprogramming; IEC 61508-7 C.5.3 interface\nchecking"];
  G31 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G31\nAn IEC 61508 method realising Sanity Check\nis implemented in backEnd, and its\neffectiveness for the faults of concern is\ndemonstrated.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G32 [shape=box label="G32\nA random hardware fault in the doer's\nprocessor does not prevent detection,\nbecause the checker runs on another\nprocessor. [low_sil_doer_checker/SC2]"];
  S14 [shape=parallelogram label="S14\nAchieved through the Replication\nRedundancy tactic (Redundancy):\nIntroduction of a redundant system which\nallows detection or masking of random\nhardware failures (not systematic\nfailures)."];
  C32 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C32\nReplication Redundancy: Introduction of a\nredundant system of the same\nimplementation. The redundant systems\nmaintain the same functionality, use\nidentical hardware, and run the same\nsoftware implementation."];
  G33 [shape=box label="G33\nIn the deployed mapping, the replicated\ncomponents are deployed on hardware that\ndoes not share a single point of random\nhardware failure."];
  Sn10 [shape=circle label="Sn10\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nDIFFERENT between backEnd and\nbackEnd/checker: cores 8/9, fault\ncontainment regions 4/4, core types\ncortexM/cortexM."];
  C33 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C33\nCandidate methods from the standard: IEC\n61508-7 A.2.1 tests by redundant hardware;\nIEC 61508-7 A.2.5 monitored redundancy;\nIEC 61508-7 A.3.5 reciprocal comparison by\nsoftware; IEC 61508-7 A.4.5 block\nreplication; IEC 61508-7 A.6.3\nmulti-channel output; IEC 61508-7 A.7.3\ncomplete hardware redundancy; IEC 61508-7\nA.7.5 transmission redundancy"];
  G34 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G34\nAn IEC 61508 method realising Replication\nRedundancy is implemented in backEnd, and\nits effectiveness for the faults of\nconcern is demonstrated.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G35 [shape=box label="G35\nNo core hosts software of differing\nintegrity without certified partitioning,\nand every core is provisioned to at least\nthe highest integrity level it hosts."];
  C34 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C34\nKoopman's rule 2: absent certified\npartitioning, all software on a processor\nmust be developed to the highest integrity\nlevel present on it. Whether a core type\ncan provide such partitioning is declared\nper core type by the platform (Q18)."];
  S15 [shape=parallelogram label="S15\nAchieved through the Barrier tactic\n(Isolation): protect a subsystem from\ninfluences of other subsystems."];
  Sn11 [shape=circle label="Sn11\nIndependent re-check of the solution: all\n22 core slots re-examined against their\ntype ceiling and against the set of\nintegrity levels actually hosted."];
  G36 [shape=box label="G36\nThe deployed mapping and static order meet\nthe declared timing requirements, in the\nfault-free and in the degraded case alike."];
  C35 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C35\nIteration period per application: [1079].\nTiming is a safety property here because a\nreplica that misses its deadline cannot\nperform the check the pattern credits it\nwith."];
  Sn12 [shape=circle label="Sn12\nIndependent re-check of the solution: the\nmapping-and-schedule-aware graph was\nrebuilt from the returned assignment and\nits period computed twice by disjoint\nmethods -- Lawler's parametric\nmaximum-cycle-ratio search and max-plus\nself-timed simulation -- which agree with\neach other, and the period the solver\nreported is the least integer at or above\nthat ratio."];
  Sn13 [shape=circle label="Sn13\nIndependent re-check of the solution: the\nreported period is at least the total\nexecution demand of the busiest core, the\nbound that a static order left open as a\nchain silently loses."];
  G37 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G37\nEvery software component is developed,\nverified and validated to its allocated\nsafety integrity level in accordance with\nIEC 61508-3.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  C36 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C36\nIntegrity levels to be discharged by\nprocess, as active component counts: SIL\n1: 4, SIL 2: 2, SIL 3: 4. Components\nimplemented above their allocated level\nwere promoted to satisfy Koopman's rule 2;\nthe cost of that promotion is what the\nexploration minimised."];
  G1 -> S1 [arrowhead=normal];
